{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Land PR #127 via Gerrit: pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2; mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs never merge there; content is re-applied\nlocally and landed via Gerrit, then the PR is closed by hand. PR #127 proposes:\n\n* `pypandoc-binary` `1.15` -> `1.17` (pinned EXACTLY, `wiki` extra + `dev` group);\n* `ruff` `0.16.1` -> `0.16.2` (pinned EXACTLY in `dev` — hook, local lint, CI identical);\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (major), loosening the pyproject ceiling `<2` -> `<3`.\n\nThe `mcp` half is the THIRD re-proposal (PRs #124/#125/#127), rejected on evidence under\nticket 1dfd (mcp 2.0 removes `mcp.server.fastmcp`, imported by `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`\nand `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`); the migration is open epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`\n(bared-nickel-insect): stay on `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` until 2.0.x stabilizes. PR #125 applied\nthe same rule (change 1483). This ticket lands the safe subset only.\n\n## Approach\n\nLand the `pypandoc-binary` + `ruff` bumps, `mcp` ceiling stays `<2` (resolver keeps\n1.29.0). In a fresh worktree branched from `origin/main`:\n\n1. `pyproject.toml`: `pypandoc-binary==1.15` -> `==1.17` in BOTH `wiki` and `dev` (the\n   notice test enforces one distinct pin value); `ruff==0.16.1` -> `==0.16.2` in `dev`.\n   Keep both pins exact.\n2. `uv lock --upgrade-package pypandoc-binary --upgrade-package ruff` — the lock is\n   regenerated by uv, never hand-edited (CI gates on `uv lock --check`); then sync the\n   venv so the new wheels are installed.\n3. **Pin-provenance consumers**: read the new BUNDLED pandoc version empirically\n   (`pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`), then update EVERY hard-coded pin site (inventory:\n   `grep -rn '3\\.6\\.1|1\\.15'` over the whole tree, excluding only uv.lock and captured\n   fixture data):\n   * `NOTICE` — the `Version:` line + the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel reference; and\n     the `\"3.6.1\" in text` assertion in `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py`.\n     Do NOT touch its upstream-URL assertion (`\"pandoc.org\" in text or ...`) — a\n     parallel change owns that exact line.\n   * `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py` — NON-skipping provenance asserts\n     `pypandoc.__version__ == \"1.15\"` (L55) + banner `pandoc 3.6.1` (L59), and ADR\n     asserts `\"3.6.1\" in adr` / `\"1.15\" in adr` (L326-327).\n   * ADR 0095 — the \"Pin provenance\" pin + bundled-pandoc line (what L326-327 read); its\n     conversion shapes are re-verified by the module's real-pandoc shape tests (shape\n     drift = baseline churn, step 4 stop rule).\n   * ADR 0096 — the Finding recording the pins + both SHA-256 fingerprints (lockstep\n     with 4b).\n   * `wiki_render.py` module docstring's `pandoc 3.6.1` mention (accuracy only).\n   * `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — hard-codes \"3.6.1\" as the\n     version passed to `validate_pandoc_provenance` while building provenance from\n     `generator.LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` (L103/111/193/201/203/247); the 4a bump makes the\n     version-match check raise, so update those literals (or derive from the constant).\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json` mentions the old pins too but is\n   captured historical ticket data — leave it byte-identical.\n4. **Byte-safety corpus**: `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` freezes\n   `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION = \"3.6.1\"` + a per-platform `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256`\n   map (darwin-arm64, linux-x86_64); test_wiki_render_hardening.py's provenance test\n   validates the installed binary's version + SHA-256 against the provenance in\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` + the three `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/`\n   files. Bumping the wheel = deliberately re-establishing the reviewed baseline (the act\n   the generator's docstring sanctions):\n   a. Update `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` to the new bundled version.\n   b. Recompute BOTH fingerprints: darwin-arm64 = SHA-256 of the locally installed\n      pandoc; linux-x86_64 = download the exact 1.17 manylinux x86_64 wheel recorded\n      (URL + hash) in `uv.lock`, extract, hash the `pandoc` inside — no Linux host\n      needed; wheel integrity is attested by uv.lock.\n   c. Regenerate the legacy manifest + three replay files with the generator (supported\n      binaries of one version emit byte-identical fixtures, so a darwin regeneration is\n      valid for CI's linux gate; the provenance test enforces this).\n   d. Confirm with the script's non-writing `--check` + test_wiki_render_hardening.py.\n   If the bytes churn implausibly (unit count deviates from 884, or `--check` disagrees),\n   STOP: defer the pypandoc half too (land ruff alone) rather than commit an unreviewed\n   baseline.\n5. **ruff verdict drift**: run `make lint`; if 0.16.2 flags or reformats existing code,\n   apply the minimal fix and note it in the commit message. NEVER touch\n   `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n6. Do NOT touch the `mcp` constraints, `_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 — 732b's edit-set.\n7. Verify (`make lint && make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit tests/scripts`, generator\n   `--check`), commit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off, push\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`; leave the ticket `in_progress` while the\n   orchestrator shepherds `LLM-Review`/`Verified`; close only after merge, with PR #127\n   closed by a comment pointing the mcp half at 732b.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `pyproject.toml` — the two `pypandoc-binary==` pins (`wiki` + `dev`) + the `dev`\n  `ruff==` pin.\n* `uv.lock` — regenerated entries + incidental churn.\n* Pin-provenance consumers (step 3): `NOTICE`, notice test (version string only, never\n  the upstream-URL line), test_wiki_render.py pin asserts, ADR 0095 \"Pin provenance\" +\n  ADR 0096 pin/fingerprint findings, `wiki_render.py` docstring,\n  `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` version literals.\n* `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` + both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` entries, nothing else.\n* `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` + three `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/`\n  files — regenerated wholesale by the generator, never hand-edited.\n* Minimal source fixes ONLY if ruff 0.16.2 changes a lint/format verdict.\n* OUT: the `mcp` bump and its `<2` -> `<3` ceiling move (deferred to epic\n  `732b-51df-acf2-477b` — already filed, no new ticket needed);\n  `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; ADR 0050; `.github/complexity-baseline.json`;\n  dependabot config; other open dependency PRs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `pyproject.toml` has `pypandoc-binary==1.17` (twice: `wiki` + `dev`),\n  `ruff==0.16.2`, and still `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` in both the `mcp` extra and `dev`\n  (`grep -nE 'pypandoc-binary==|ruff==|mcp>=' pyproject.toml`).\n- [ ] AC2: `uv.lock` records pypandoc-binary 1.17, ruff 0.16.2, mcp 1.29.0\n  (`grep -A1 -E '^name = \"(pypandoc-binary|ruff|mcp)\"$' uv.lock`) and `uv lock --check`\n  exits 0 (the same gate CI runs).\n- [ ] AC3: every pin-provenance consumer names the versions 1.17 actually ships (per\n  `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`): `NOTICE`, the notice test's version string,\n  test_wiki_render.py's provenance asserts, ADR 0095 Pin provenance, ADR 0096\n  fingerprints; `pytest tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py` exits 0 (non-skipping).\n- [ ] AC4: baseline re-established: `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` + both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` fingerprints match the 1.17 wheels (darwin from the\n  installed binary, linux from the uv.lock-pinned manylinux x86_64 wheel), fixtures are\n  regenerated by the script (never hand-edited),\n  `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py --check` exits 0, and\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint` (ruff 0.16.2), `make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit`, and\n  `pytest tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` all exit 0 with the\n  worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n- [ ] AC6: a Gerrit change carrying this diff exists on refs/for/main with this\n  ticket's `rebar-ticket:` trailer and DCO sign-off (`git log -1 --format=%B HEAD`).\n- [ ] AC7: the mcp 2.0 half is NOT landed (no edit to the `mcp` constraints,\n  `_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 per `git diff origin/main --stat`), and the deferral is\n  recorded as a ticket comment naming epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786806531106061001,"uuid":"1db0e404-b621-429f-961a-96159ca7c39d"}